From 42d1581ec33dea4efb1d77b60e10d4ce5a711654 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:17:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Offer texture arrays to compute kernels under the own
 Vulkan backend (native GPU plan 5.2a)

Where the device has descriptor indexing (runtime arrays, variable descriptor
counts and non-uniform indexing of sampled images), a compute pipeline can
read one array of sampled textures from set 3, sized when it is bound.
Gpu_Caps.texture_arrays says how many one array may hold (exit stat
texture_arrays=), 0 under SDL_GPU, Metal or a device without the features.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RvkVmjYXFP4g5FN7pGhnXm
